{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Second change committed as 2b27423f8b6 on b6-antbear-decisions (base main b0d2da19538, plan review PASS certified at that sha). (a) janitor: _evict returns None (deferred) when the rename fails with the entry present; GcResult.deferred; reverify_entry raises SnapshotEntryInUseError for an unmovable corrupt entry; the reverify pass counts that as deferred and skips entries the reclaim loop already deferred (one deferral per entry per pass, from review advisory G6); startup_sweep untouched. (b) 3 peak-RSS tests expect None without resource, plus a test hiding resource on every platform. (c) 0o600 assertion gated on os.name != 'nt' citing cloistered-decomposed-nymph; the 0o600 check is intentionally unsupported on Windows, and the rest of the test now runs there. posix-api.args now holds only test_certifies_when_the_key_dir_is_read_only (intentionally unsupported, recorded earlier). macOS: 83 snapshot tests + peak RSS/op-cert/deselect-parity tests pass; make lint and typecheck clean; mechanism ratchet exit 0. Local red check: with only janitor.py reverted, the 5 deferral tests fail (open-reader test on an assertion). Windows dispatches 2026-11-23 10:33 PST: pass run 45239611331 (tmp/b6-antbear-pass at 2b27423f8b6), red control run 45239618515 (tmp/b6-antbear-red at 92a4191d7c5 = janitor.py reverted, tests kept). make verify running."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795458850629795001,"uuid":"66153d39-f3db-4d91-9f50-1b9775d2ee17"}